UPDATE companies SET description='Marpac Medical operates from Albuquerque, New Mexico, where it has produced medical devices since its spin-off from Rotec in 1992. Rotec began in the 1980s manufacturing tracheostomy tube holders and orthopedic products for DePuy; when DePuy acquired the orthopedic division, the tracheostomy holder business became the privately held Marpac.

The company manufactures FDA Class 1 medical devices, specifically endotracheal (ET) tube holders and tracheostomy tube holders. All products are designed and produced at its Albuquerque facility without outsourcing, a structure the company says allows strict quality control and rapid response to customer needs. Marpac aims to keep all items in stock and typically ships orders within one to two days.

Its distributor network includes New Start Home Medical Equipment, Timberlake Medical, Affordable Medical Supply, and Medical Specialties Distributors.

Founded on principles of quality, affordability, innovation, and customer service, Marpac was created to develop products that improve patient care while remaining easy for medical staff and families to use.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Medical device manufacturing", "FDA Class 1 device production", "ET tube holder manufacturing", "Tracheostomy tube holder manufacturing", "In-house design and production", "Quality control"], "industries": ["Medical equipment manufacturing", "Healthcare supplies", "Home medical equipment", "Medical device distribution"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Typically ships orders within 1-2 days", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Products designed and manufactured in the USA with no outsourcing", "Strict quality control through in-house production", "Typically ships orders within 1-2 days", "Strives to keep all products in stock", "Focus on quality, affordability, innovation, and customer service"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Albuquerque, New Mexico -> db", "Founded as Rotec in 1980s, spun off as Marpac in 1992 -> /about-us", "Privately held company -> /about-us", "Manufactures FDA Class 1 medical devices (ET Tube and Tracheostomy Tube Holders) -> /about-us", "Products designed and produced in USA at Albuquerque facility, no outsourcing -> /about-us", "Typically ships orders within 1-2 days -> /about-us", "Serves medical community, hospitals, medical staff, families -> /about-us", "Distributors include New Start Home Medical Equipment, Timberlake Medical, Affordable Medical Supply, Medical Specialties Distributors -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "As a medical supply manufacturer of FDA Class 1 medical device such as ET Tube and Tracheostomy Tube Holders", "founded_year": "1992", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='marpac-medical' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Mars Plastics operates from Providence, Rhode Island, with a second facility in nearby Cranston. The company has over 50 years of injection molding experience and remains a family-owned business passed through generations. Founded as a molding operation, it has grown into one of the largest injection molders on the East Coast, serving customers ranging from individual inventors to major retailers.

The company runs a 100,000-square-foot facility operating 24 hours a day, seven days a week. Its equipment lineup includes 40 injection molding machines — 36 in Providence and four in Cranston — ranging from 12 to 1,400 tons of clamping force with shot capacities up to 160 ounces. Core processes cover conventional injection molding, gas-assist molding, over-molding, insert molding, and two-color molding. In-house capabilities extend to tool design and machining, design engineering with CAD and simulation, finishing (trimming, painting, printing, plating), assembly, and work-cell manufacturing that integrates decorating and packaging. A recent addition is 3D printing for rapid prototyping and low-volume production.

Mars Plastics serves retail giants such as Target and Walmart as an authorized manufacturer, along with a broad base of corporate clients and startup inventors. The company has helped numerous small concepts scale into industry leaders and has guided established corporations in reshoring production from overseas to its Rhode Island plants. Its contract manufacturing services support third-party brands across consumer goods and other sectors.

The company emphasizes a dedicated inside representative for every customer, continuous reinvestment in new molding machines and robotic automation, and a quality system that retains first and last shots from each run alongside statistical process control. Work-cell manufacturing is cited as a key differentiator that allows Mars to compete with overseas facilities on cost and lead time.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Plastic injection molding", "Gas-assist injection molding", "Over-molding", "Insert molding", "Two-color molding", "Work-cell manufacturing", "Assembly", "Finishing (trimming, painting, printing, plating)", "Tooling design and machining", "Design and engineering (CAD, simulation)", "3D printing (rapid prototyping)", "Reshoring/onshoring services", "Contract manufacturing", "Quality assurance (SPC, first/last shot retention)"], "industries": ["Retail (Target, Walmart)", "Consumer products", "Inventors/startups", "Major corporations", "Contract manufacturing"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["40 injection molding machines (12\u20131,400 tons, up to 160 oz shot capacity)", "Gas-assist injection molding machines (800\u20131,200 tons, up to 180 oz)", "Robotic production cells", "3D printing equipment", "In-house tooling design and machining centers"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Dedicated inside representative assigned to each customer", "Work-cell manufacturing integrating molding, assembly, decorating, and packaging", "40 injection molding machines (12\u20131,400 tons, up to 160 oz shot capacity) across two Rhode Island facilities", "24/7 production in a 100,000 sq ft facility with continuous machine reinvestment", "Authorized manufacturer for Target and Walmart"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Providence, Rhode Island -> db", "Second facility in Cranston, RI -> /about-us", "Over 50 years molding experience -> /about-us", "Family-owned business -> /about-us", "One of largest injection molders on East Coast -> /about-us", "40 injection molding machines (36 Providence, 4 Cranston) -> /about-us", "Machine range 12\u20131,400 tons, shot capacity up to 160 oz -> /about-us", "100,000 sq ft facility, 24/7 operation -> /services", "Gas-assist molding machines 800\u20131,200 tons up to 180 oz -> /services", "Processes: over-mold, insert molding, two-color molding -> /about-us", "Work-cell manufacturing with assembly, decorating, packaging -> /about-us, /services", "In-house tooling design and machining -> /services", "Design and engineering with CAD/simulation -> /services", "Finishing: trimming, painting, printing, plating -> /services", "3D printing services for prototyping and low volume -> /services", "Reshoring/onshoring expertise -> /services", "Contract manufacturing services -> /services", "Authorized manufacturer for Target and Walmart -> /", "Quality assurance: SPC, first/last shot retention -> /services", "Robotic production technology -> /services", "Continuous reinvestment in new machines -> /services", "Dedicated inside representative per customer -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Mars Plastics is one of the largest plastic injection molders on the east coast.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='mars-plastics' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Martel Inc was founded on July 2, 1984, in Dover, Delaware, by Mark B. Carlson. The family-owned company began as a one-man operation out of a garage, aiming to provide reliable telecommunications solutions for businesses on the Delmarva Peninsula.

Today, Martel operates from a commercial facility in Dover with a fully stocked parts warehouse and offers 24/7 service. The company provides cloud-based VOIP, legacy telecommunications, video surveillance systems, access control, and structured cabling for computer and telephone networks. A full staff of technicians and sales personnel handles installation, maintenance, and support.

Martel serves businesses across Delmarva and southeastern Pennsylvania, including clients such as Delaware Grange Mutual Insurance Company, Parsell Funeral Homes & Crematorium, Surgical Associates, and the Delaware Surgery Center. Its customer base spans industries needing commercial phone systems, security cameras, legacy telecom, and network cabling.

