r block and front-faced countertops mentioned in testimonial -> page /", "Customer testimonials referencing custom orders, quality, and service -> page /"], "company_type": "Retailer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "They also make custom butcher block and front faced countertops in multiple hardwoods at great prices.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='martin-s-furniture' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Maryland Community Solar operates from Columbia, Maryland, as a locally owned, family-run enterprise led by CEO Tony Napolitano. The company was established to educate Maryland residents and businesses about community solar programs and to simplify enrollment in those programs.

The firm provides consumer education on the benefits of community solar, assesses eligibility, and guides customers through the enrollment process. A customer relations team works directly with homeowners, renters, and businesses, including those served by third-party energy suppliers, to explain how subscription to a local solar farm can reduce electric bills by 5% to 25%. The company reports assisting hundreds of customers across the state.

Services are directed at Maryland residential and commercial utility customers who cannot install rooftop panels, such as condominium dwellers, as well as businesses seeking renewable energy credits. The company coordinates with solar developers and utility providers to facilitate the subscription and billing process.

The organization states its mission is to make Maryland a leader in sustainability and renewable energy through honest communication, by example, and caring for customers and communities.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Community solar program education", "Eligibility assessment and enrollment assistance", "Customer relations and support", "Renewable energy credit subscription facilitation"], "industries": ["Renewable energy", "Community solar"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Locally owned, family-run operation", "Direct, in-person customer relations team", "Assistance for customers with third-party energy suppliers", "Mission-driven focus on state-wide sustainability leadership"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Columbia, Maryland -> db", "Family-owned, locally owned -> /about-us", "CEO Tony Napolitano -> /about-us", "Educates consumers and businesses about community solar benefits and helps enroll -> /about-us", "Customer relations team assists with enrollment -> /", "Helps hundreds of people join community solar -> /about-us", "Serves residential and commercial customers, including those with third-party suppliers -> /, /about-us", "Mission to make Maryland a leader in sustainability and renewable energy -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Other", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Maryland Community Solar educates consumers and businesses about the benefits of community solar programs and helps them enroll in the program that''s right for them.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='maryland-community-solar' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='The Maryland Food Center Authority (MFCA) operates from Jessup, Maryland, where it oversees the Maryland Food Center, a centralized hub for wholesale food distribution.

The authority manages two primary facilities—the Maryland Wholesale Produce Market and the Maryland Market Center—leasing space to a roster of wholesale merchants selling fruits, vegetables, and seafood.

The center serves the broader food industry, including wholesale produce distributors, seafood suppliers, and a single retail seafood vendor open to the public. Tenants such as Pro Produce, C&D Produce, Sweet Seasons Maryland, War Shore Trading Company, Wild Seafood, and Viva Food operate within the leased units, distributing products regionally.

