e, production, assembly, testing, conformal coating, box build -> /services", "Certifications: ISO 9001:2015, IPC-A-610 Class 2, IPC J-STD-001, RoHS/REACH -> /quality", "Industries served: commercial electronics, consumer devices, telecommunications, healthcare/medical devices, industrial equipment -> /about-us", "No order minimums -> /", "Production volume: hundreds to tens of thousands -> /services", "Equipment: 3D AOI, X-ray, AOI -> /quality", "Domestic manufacturing in Wisconsin -> /", "One partner every stage under one roof -> /services"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Matrix Corp is a Wisconsin-based contract electronics manufacturer building printed circuit boards from single-unit prototypes through low-to-mid volume production", "founded_year": "1999", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "No minimum order quantity", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='matrix-corporation' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Maverick Power is headquartered in McKinney, Texas. The company was founded in 2020 as RMS Power by Tom Currier, Chad Dodd, John Baker, and Timmy Brent before evolving into the Maverick Power brand. The founders set out to redefine mission‑critical power solutions with a client‑first approach born from the challenges of that year.

The company designs and manufactures a range of power distribution equipment, including automatic transfer switches, medium‑voltage switchgear (1 kV to 36 kV), low‑voltage distribution systems (up to 1 kV), UL 508A‑listed industrial control panels, and uninterruptible power supply units with maintenance bypass. In addition to manufacturing, Maverick Power provides installation, maintenance and repair, consulting, field services, and full project management. Operations span multiple manufacturing facilities across North Texas and Phoenix, and the firm was ranked #16 on the 2025 Inc. 5000 list, #2 in Manufacturing and #1 in Texas.

Maverick Power serves data centers, critical‑infrastructure operators, industrial automation users, energy‑management firms, and commercial and industrial facilities that require reliable, customizable power distribution. Its solutions are built for mission‑critical environments where uptime and rapid deployment are essential.

