UPDATE companies SET description='MedEquip Depot, based in Dallas, Texas, operates as an authorized distributor of medical supplies, equipment, and furniture for healthcare facilities nationwide. The company holds SAM.gov registration (CAGE 6H2R8), a Vizient contract, and a Texas Department of Health license, positioning it for federal and institutional procurement.

The distributor consolidates products from more than 1,300 manufacturers under a single account, serving over 13,000 healthcare facilities across every clinical specialty. Its Dallas warehouse facility and direct-from-manufacturer shipping options support a catalog that spans capital equipment, clinical furniture, and daily consumables. Services include custom procedure kit assembly, real-time order tracking through a customer portal, volume pricing negotiations with manufacturers, and consolidated invoicing with Net-30 terms for qualifying institutions.

Customers range from hospitals, ambulatory surgery centers, and physician practices to dental clinics, veterinary hospitals, long-term care communities, and government agencies. The company also supports distributors, educational institutions, first responders, and commercial occupational health programs. Each sector receives dedicated quoting, order management, and account support tailored to its procurement workflows.

Its model emphasizes a dedicated account team that knows each facility’s receiving dock, manufacturer-negotiated pricing on volume orders, multiple sourcing channels for backordered items, and transparent lead-time quoting that avoids vague estimates. Custom kits are built to exact component specifications, and a returns-and-claims team handles substitutions and freight claims in writing.', certifications=ARRAY['SAM.gov registration','Vizient contract','Provista contract']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Medical supply distribution", "Medical equipment distribution", "Clinical furniture distribution", "Custom procedure kit assembly", "Consolidated vendor management", "Real-time order tracking", "Volume pricing negotiation", "Government procurement support (SAM, Vizient)", "Net-30 invoicing", "Price matching", "Free ground shipping on qualifying orders", "Multiple sourcing channels", "Custom kit packaging (trays, pouches, bags)", "Manufacturer lead time quoting", "Quick reorder system", "Returns, exchanges, and claims management"], "industries": ["Hospitals and acute care", "Ambulatory surgery centers", "Physician practices", "Specialty clinics (cardiology, orthopedics, dermatology, OBGYN, oncology, pain management, podiatry, urology, ophthalmology, ENT, neurology, endocrinology, gastroenterology, dialysis, wound care, sleep medicine, radiology, physical therapy, aesthetic surgery, pediatrics, diagnostic laboratories)", "Dental practices", "Veterinary clinics", "Skilled nursing facilities", "Long-term care homes", "Assisted living", "Hospice organizations", "Memory care communities", "Behavioral health centers", "Substance use rehabilitation facilities", "DME suppliers", "Pharmacies", "Medical transport providers", "EMS first responders", "Home healthcare agencies", "Biomedical engineering teams", "Surgical reprocessing facilities", "Clinical environmental services", "Medical waste management", "Regional distributors", "Medical equipment resellers", "Healthcare 