UPDATE companies SET description='Medical Armor Corporation operates from Fremont, Nebraska, where it has developed and supplied its signature Kevlar surgical underglove for more than three decades.

The device carries FDA 510(k) clearance and is produced domestically. Each glove can be re-sterilized and reused up to five additional times, yielding a total of six uses per unit. The company does not publish facility size, headcount, or annual volume figures.

Primary customers include orthopedic surgeons, podiatric surgeons, pathology labs, paramedics, emergency-room staff, and fire and police personnel. Beyond healthcare, the gloves are used in advanced manufacturing, sheet metal work, automotive repair, glass handling, mortuary and coroner services, and home and garden tasks.

