UPDATE companies SET description='Metal Doctors operates from East Providence, Rhode Island. The shop was founded by Frank, a metalworker with over three decades of experience who began his career at his father-in-law''s metal shop, eventually running that operation before striking out on his own. Frank handles every project himself, from intake to finish, with no team handoffs.

The shop specializes in metal restoration and custom fabrication across a range of metals including brass, copper, steel, aluminum, zinc, and white metal — with a noted specialty in white and pot metal that few shops handle. Services span complete body restoration and panel fabrication for rare vehicles, rust repair, period-correct finishing, custom architectural elements, bespoke furniture, decorative art, railings, gates, specialized tooling, and prototype development. Welding capabilities cover TIG, MIG, stick, brazing, and soldering for aluminum, stainless steel, cast iron, and other alloys, with mobile welding available for on-site repairs. Frank works alone, so every piece moves through the shop under a single pair of hands.

Clients include antique and classic vehicle owners, vintage furniture collectors, museums, private collections, and residential and commercial customers needing architectural metalwork. The shop has restored items such as a rusted dump trailer and a rusted-through floor pan, and its work has gone to museums and private collections as well as local individuals.

The company distinguishes itself through its willingness to tackle white metal and pot metal repairs that most shops decline, and through Frank''s solo-craftsman model that eliminates handoffs. Other metalworkers reportedly bring him repairs they cannot complete, and he applies the same care to museum pieces as to neighborhood projects.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Metal restoration", "Complete body restoration and panel fabrication", "Rust repair and metal preservation", "Custom metal parts fabrication for rare vehicles", "Precision welding for structural integrity", "Period-correct metal finishing techniques", "Metal furniture repair and restoration", "Structural reinforcement while maintaining original design", "Metal cleaning, refinishing, and repainting", "Hardware replacement, repair, and reproduction", "Custom architectural metal elements and fixtures", "Bespoke furniture and decorative metal art", "Commercial and residential railings and gates", "Specialized tools and equipment fabrication", "Prototype development and one-off pieces", "TIG welding", "MIG welding", "Stick welding", "Aluminum welding", "Stainless steel welding", "Cast iron welding", "Brazing and soldering", "Mobile welding services", "Structural and ornamental welding"], "industries": ["Antique vehicle restoration", "Vintage furniture restoration", "Classic car restoration", "Rare vehicle restoration", "Museum conservation", "Private collections", "Architectural metalwork", "Custom metal fabrication", "Antique hardware restoration"], "materials": ["Brass", "Copper", "Steel", "Aluminum", "Zinc", "White metal", "Pot metal", "Stainless steel", "Cast iron"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["White metal and pot metal restoration specialty", "Solo craftsman model \u2014 no handoffs, one person start to finish", "Mobile welding for on-site repairs", "Period-correct metal finishing techniques", "Handles repairs other shops turn away"], "facts_used": ["Location: East Providence, RI -> db", "Founder: Frank, over 30 years experience, started at father-in-law''s shop, ran it, then started Metal Doctors -> /", "Solo operation: Frank handles every piece himself, no team -> /", "Metals worked: brass, copper, steel, aluminum, zinc, white metal, pot metal -> /", "Specialty: white metal and pot metal restoration -> /", "Services: metal restoration, custom fabrication, welding (TIG, MIG, stick, brazing, soldering), mobile welding -> /", "Specific capabilities: complete body restoration, panel fabrication, rust repair, period-correct finishing, architectural elements, furniture, decorative art, railings, gates, tooling, prototypes -> /", "Industries: antique/classic/rare vehicles, vintage furniture, museums, private collections, architectural metalwork -> /", "Differentiators: white/pot metal specialty, solo craftsman, mobile welding, period-correct finishes, takes jobs others decline -> /", "Materials: brass, copper, steel, aluminum, zinc, white metal, pot metal, stainless steel, cast iron -> /", "Company type: contract manufacturer/job shop (custom fabrication, restoration, welding for clients) -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We repair and restore all metals \u2014 brass, copper, steel, aluminum, zinc, and white metal. From antique hardware to custom fabrication.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='metal-doctors' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Metal Fabricators of St. Louis operates from St. Louis, Missouri, where it was founded in 1986. The business has maintained a focus on sheet metal fabrication and precision weldments since its founding.

The shop specializes in precision weldments and sheet metal fabrication, offering a range of in-house processes: laser cutting, forming, sawing and machining, welding and fitting, and finishing services that include powder coating and wet spray. The company’s website presents each service with detailed views, and it emphasizes that each sheet metal piece leaves its fabrication shop meeting standards of accuracy and reliability. Facility size, headcount, and annual volume are not published.

The company does not specify target industries or customer types in its public materials, nor does it list specific client examples.

The business was built on three core attributes—accuracy, quality, and reliability—and states that it stands behind every product by never wavering from those principles, which serve as its motto and founding philosophy. The company’s description reinforces that these attributes are the foundation upon which it was founded. The motto appears prominently on its website alongside service listings.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Laser Cutting", "Forming", "Sawing / Machining", "Welding / Fitting", "Finishing Services", "Powder Coating / Wet Spray"], "industries": [], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Founding attributes of accuracy, quality, and reliability", "In-house laser cutting, forming, sawing/machining, welding/fitting, and finishing", "Powder coating and wet spray finishing capabilities", "Precision weldments and sheet metal fabrication focus"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1986 -> db", "Headquartered in St. Louis, Missouri -> db", "Offers laser cutting, forming, sawing/machining, welding/fitting, finishing services, powder coating/wet spray -> page \"/\"", "Motto: Accuracy, Quality, Reliability -> page \"/\"", "Company stands behind products based on three founding attributes -> page \"/\"", "Specializes in precision weldments and sheet metal fabrication -> page \"/\"", "LinkedIn profile: https://www.linkedin.com/company/metalfabstl/ -> db", "Website: https://www.metalfabstl.com/ -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Metal Fabricators of St. Louis ensures accuracy and quality as well as the reliability of each sheet metal piece once it leaves our fabrication shop.", "founded_year": "1986", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/metalfabstl/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='metal-fabricators-of-st-louis' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Metal Industries, Inc. operates from Hartford, Connecticut, where it has been machining parts since the 1940s. The business began as Metropolitan Tool and Machine Company, founded by Vincent D. Zito at the current location on Wethersfield Avenue. The company produced components for U.S. troops during World War II. Vincent A. Zito took over in the 1950s and incorporated the firm as Metal Industries, Inc. in 1965. The shop later manufactured radiator cooling components for the Mercury Space Program space suits from 1958 to 1963. Today, the third generation, led by Vincent M. Zito, runs the operation.

The facility functions as a full-service machine shop equipped with CNC and manual lathes capable of 36-inch diameter and 17-foot length, 4-axis CNC and manual milling machines, and surface, OD, and ID grinders. It offers precision machining, engineered metal and ceramic coatings (including oxy-acetylene powder, twin arc metallizing, Rokide, and plasma arc processes), welding and fabrication (MIG, TIG, stick, brazing, silver soldering), component repair, reverse engineering, short- and long-run production, and two-plane dynamic balancing. Materials processed include steel, aluminum, bronze, plastics, and composites.

Customers span commercial, municipal, government, industrial, and agricultural sectors, with historical work for the aerospace industry on the Mercury program. The shop serves OEMs, provides spare parts, and handles repairs for hard-to-find components, offering emergency service outside normal hours to reduce downtime.

The company emphasizes its third-generation experience, creative problem-solving, and precise workmanship as differentiators, aiming to exceed expectations on jobs of any size.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["CNC and manual turning (up to 36\" diameter \u00d7 17 ft)", "4-axis CNC and manual milling", "Surface, OD, and ID grinding", "Two-plane soft suspension dynamic balancing", "MIG, TIG, stick, brazing, and silver soldering welding", "Oxy-acetylene powder and twin arc metallized coatings", "Rokide and plasma arc ceramic coatings", "Anti-wear ceramic coatings for seal and packing areas", "Abradable coatings for high and low sealing applications", "Traction/grip coatings for hazardous traffic areas and ladder rungs", "Traction coatings for drive and feed rollers", "Zinc/aluminum anti-corrosion coatings", "Component repair and refurbishment", "Reverse engineering and replicated parts", "Short- and long-run contract manufacturing", "Engineering and design support", "Emergency after-hours service"], "industries": ["Commercial", "Municipal", "Government", "Industrial", "Agricultural", "Aerospace"], "materials": ["Steel", "Aluminum", "Bronze", "Plastics", "Composites"], "equipment": ["CNC and manual lathes (36\" diameter \u00d7 17 ft)", "4-axis CNC and manual milling machines", "Surface grinders", "OD grinders", "ID grinders", "Two-plane soft suspension dynamic balancing equipment", "Oxy-acetylene powder coating system", "Twin arc metallizing equipment", "Rokide ceramic coating system", "Plasma arc ceramic coating system"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Emergency services available during and after business hours to minimize customer downtime", "Third-generation family ownership with over 80 years of combined hands-on machine shop experience", "Metallized coating processes that reclaim worn or mis-machined components to original specifications", "Reverse engineering and replication of obsolete or hard-to-find 