UPDATE companies SET description='Metal Solutions Design & Fabrication, LLC operates from Dayton, Kentucky. The company was founded in 2005 when three separate businesses combined their knowledge and experience to create a multi-faceted metal design and fabrication firm. No individual founders are named in public materials.

The shop functions as a production job shop offering custom fabrication and welding, stair systems, handrails and guardrails, ornamental ironwork, D.O.T.-certified IP-1, IP-2 and 7A Type A shipping containers, structural steel systems, ground support systems, machine bases and guarding, precision forming and powder coating. Engineers use SolidWorks 3D software to provide accelerated design services, FEA modeling and analysis, and general engineering support. The facility operates under an NQA-1 (2012 edition) quality assurance program with in-house certified welding inspectors.

Customers span shipping and transportation, aerospace and defense, architecture and construction, entertainment venues, nuclear and power plants, industrial machine builders, material handling and technology sectors. Concrete clients include the U.S. military, NASA, Disney, Paramount, the Department of Energy, national laboratories and power generation firms. The company also serves industrial process designers, conveyor designers and food handling equipment manufacturers.

The founders aimed to create a "one-stop shop" for design and manufacturing needs, emphasizing quicker lead times than overseas sourcing. The company highlights its NQA-1 program, in-house CWI staff, D.O.T. testing and certification services, and quick turn-around times as key differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY['NQA-1 (2012 edition)','D.O.T. IP-1','D.O.T. IP-2','D.O.T. 7A Type A','Certified Welding Inspector (CWI)']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom fabrication & welding", "Stair systems", "Handrails & guardrails", "Ornamental ironwork", "D.O.T. certified shipping containers (IP-1, IP-2, 7A Type A)", "Structural steel systems", "Ground support systems", "Machine bases and guarding", "Precision forming", "Powder coating", "Accelerated design services (SolidWorks 3D)", "Engineering services", "FEA modeling and analysis", "D.O.T. Testing and Certification Services", "CNC press brake operation", "Welding inspection (CWI)", "NQA-1 quality assurance"], "industries": ["Shipping & Transportation", "Aerospace & Defense", "Architecture & Construction", "Entertainment Venues", "Nuclear & Power Plants", "Industrial Machine Builders", "Material Handling", "Technology"], "materials": ["Steel", "Structural steel", "Iron"], "equipment": ["CNC press brake machines"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["NQA-1 Quality Assurance Program (2012 edition)", "In-house Certified Welding Inspectors (CWI)", "D.O.T. Testing and Certification Services", "Accelerated design services using SolidWorks 3D", "Quick turn-around times"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2005 by combining three businesses -> /about", "Headquarters Dayton, Kentucky -> db", "NQA-1 (2012 edition) quality program -> /, /about", "In-house Certified Welding Inspectors (CWI) -> /", "D.O.T. Testing and Certification Services -> /, /about", "Accelerated design services using SolidWorks 3D -> /, /about", "Services: custom fabrication & welding, stair systems, handrails & guardrails, ornamental ironwork, D.O.T. certified shipping containers, structural steel, ground support, machine bases, precision forming, powder coating -> /about", "Industries served: Shipping & Transportation, Aerospace & Defense, Architecture & Construction, Entertainment Venues, Nuclear & Power Plants, Industrial Machine Builders, Material Handling, Technology -> /", "Customers: U.S. military, NASA, Disney, Paramount, DOE, National Laboratories, Power Gen -> /", "CNC press brake machines used -> / (job posting)", "Mission: one-stop shop for design and manufacturing -> /, /about"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "While we are a production job shop, we continue to enhance our ability to deliver accelerated design services prior to fabrication.", "founded_year": "2005", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='metal-solutions-design-fabrication-llc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Metal Standard Corporation was founded in 1945 in Holland, Michigan. The company has operated continuously since then as a metal fabrication specialist.

The company focuses on high-volume welded tubular steel and wire-formed products. Its capabilities include tube and sheet metal laser cutting, tube bending (left and right hand), wire forming, roll bending, manual welding, brazing, and precision robotic welding with single- and dual-head robots on multi-axis positioners. A dedicated weld testing laboratory uses CMM, VMM, and Faro Arm laser equipment to verify weld penetration, strength, and dimensional accuracy. The facility processes raw, powder-coated, and plated tubular steel, sheet metal, and spooled wire sourced from certified suppliers.

Metal Standard serves original equipment manufacturers in the furniture, medical, and educational markets. Its fabricated metal components are used in products for those sectors, with the company positioning itself as an OEM supplier of metal fabricated parts.

