UPDATE companies SET description='MetalWork Austin operates from a shop at 2000 S. 7th Street in Austin, Texas. The company was founded by Ryan Scott‑Nairns, who serves as owner and founder, and employs a small team including fabricators Jake Black and Will Kozak, administrative coordinator Marie Nairns, and apprentice Trevor Norton.

The shop provides full‑service, turn‑key metal fabrication, handling design, welding, CNC plasma cutting, finishing, installation, and forging/blacksmithing. Its CNC plasma table cuts up to 3/4‑inch steel, and the welders work with steel, stainless steel, aluminum, brass, bronze, and copper. Finishing capabilities range from seamless weld sanding to patinas, powder coats, clear coats, and buffed wax. The team of five produces custom furniture, railings, signs, gates, and exterior metalwork.

Clients include home owners, business owners, architects, and interior designers. Projects span residential and commercial architectural metalwork, such as custom railings for homes, signage for businesses, and decorative gates for property entrances.

MetalWork Austin distinguishes itself by taking on unconventional designs and offering in‑house design support—from hand sketches to 3D models—so customers without technical drawings can still realize complex ideas. The company also emphasizes finish quality, stating that finish work separates good metalwork from astonishing metalwork, and it maintains old‑world forging techniques alongside modern CNC processes.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom metal fabrication", "Design (hand-drawn, 2D, 3D)", "Consultation", "Welding (all methods)", "Finishing (sanding, patinas, powder coating, clear coats, buffed wax)", "Installation", "CNC plasma cutting", "Forging & blacksmithing"], "industries": ["Home owners", "Business owners", "Architects", "Interior designers"], "materials": ["Steel", "Stainless Steel", "Aluminum", "Brass", "Bronze", "Copper"], "equipment": ["CNC plasma table (cuts up to 3/4\" steel)"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "8-12 weeks to begin work on new projects", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Full-service turn-key fabrication from design through installation", "CNC plasma cutting up to 3/4\" steel with design file assistance", "Welding expertise across steel, stainless, aluminum, brass, bronze, copper", "Specialized finishing: blackened steel, patinas, powder coats, clear coats, buffed wax", "Forging and blacksmithing for traditional textures and forms"], "facts_used": ["Location: Austin, Texas -> /", "Founder: Ryan Scott-Nairns -> /", "Team members: Jake Black, Will Kozak, Marie Nairns, Trevor Norton -> /", "Services: full service turn-key metal fabrication -> /services", "Materials: Steel, Stainless Steel, Aluminum, Brass, Bronze, Copper -> /services", "Lead time: 8-12 weeks -> /", "CNC plasma table cutting up to 3/4\" steel -> /services", "Finishing techniques: blackened steel, patinas, powder coats, clear coats -> /services", "Forging & blacksmithing capabilities -> /services", "Client types: Home Owner, Business Owner, Architect/Designer, Interior Designer -> /", "Shop address: 2000 S. 7th St, Austin TX 78704 -> /", "Shop hours: Monday-Thursday 7:00 a.m. - 4:00 p.m. -> /", "Design capabilities: hand-drawn, 2D, 3D -> /services"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "MetalWork Austin provides full service, Turn-Key metal fabrication.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "5", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='metalwork-austin' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Metaltech Products Inc. operates from Lebanon, Missouri, where Darrel and Dana Bishop founded the company in 1998. With a $76,000 loan they built a 4,000‑square‑foot shop, equipped it with a hydraulic ironworker, band saw, MIG and TIG welders, a drill press and hand tools, and hired their first fabricator, Tony Evans. The business remains family‑owned; the Bishops’ sons, Blake and Brice, now work in the operation.

The shop provides full‑cycle custom metal fabrication: design and product development, laser cutting, punch‑press and automated sawing, forming on four press brakes, CNC and manual machining, MIG, TIG, robotic MIG (GMAW) and resistance spot welding, powder coating for parts up to 26 feet long, and assembly. Quality is managed under ISO 9001:2015, and welding personnel hold American Welding Society certifications.

Metaltech serves OEM manufacturers across a range of sectors, including automotive, furniture and appliance makers—industries specifically noted for spot‑welded components. Customers engage the company for everything from concept sketches and prototypes to production‑volume component parts and pre‑assembled sub‑assemblies.

Darrel Bishop started the company after an outsourcing team at Electrovert and recognizing a gap in the supply of large machine frames. The stated mission emphasizes innovation, continuous improvement and profitability, delivered through a documented quality system and a workforce that includes second‑generation family members.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','AWS Certified Welding']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom Design", "Product Development", "Prototyping", "Laser Cutting", "Punch Press", "Automated Sawing", "Forming (Press Brake)", "CNC Machining", "Manual Machining", "MIG Welding", "TIG Welding", "Robotic MIG Welding (GMAW)", "Resistance Spot Welding", "Powder Coating", "Assembly", "Regional Delivery", "LTL Shipping", "Drop Shipping"], "industries": ["OEM Manufacturing", "Automotive", "Furniture", "Appliance"], "materials": ["Stainless Steel", "Mild Steel", "High-Strength Low-Alloy Steel (HSLA)", "Titanium", "Aluminum", "Copper", "Polycarbonates"], "equipment": ["Hydraulic Ironworker", "Band Saw", "MIG Welder", "TIG Welder", "Drill Press", "Press Brakes (4)", "Laser Cutting Machine", "Robotic Welding Cell", "Powder Coating System (26 ft capacity)", "Punch Presses"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family-owned since 1998 with second-generation leadership", "ISO 9001:2015 certified quality management system", "AWS-certified welding technicians and robotic welding operators", "In-house powder coating for parts up to 26 feet long", "Regional delivery within 300 miles plus LTL and drop-ship options"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1998 by Darrel and Dana Bishop -> /about", "Family-owned, second generation (Blake and Brice) -> /about", "Initial 4,000 sq ft facility, equipment list -> /about", "ISO 9001:2015 certification obtained 2009 -> /about", "AWS certified welding technicians and robotic operators -> /", "Powder coating system handles parts up to 26 ft -> /", "Facility expansions: 60,000 sq ft by 2008, additional 113